{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And divinations in their hand.</b> From here it follows that Balaam was a diviner, for they brought divinations in their hand so that he would not be able to put them off and say, 'I do not now have the instruments of divination.' And some interpret וקסמים as ושכר קסמים — 'and the fee of divinations' — that is, they brought him silver and gold as his fee."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:53.051223229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}